<<2>> Give me a combination of a sequence completion and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving sequence completion.
<<2>> Write the next three terms of the sequence: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, \_\_\_\_\_, \_\_\_\_\_, \_\_\_\_\_.

\begin{equation*}
\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}
\hline
\text{Term} & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8 \\
\hline
\text{Value} & 3 & 6 & 9 & 12 & 15 & & & \\
\hline
\end{array}
\end{equation*}
<<3>> Give me a "always sometimes or never true" exercise for a 4th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on even and odd numbers.
<<3>> Write the appropriate answer: Always, Sometimes, or Never

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item An even number plus an even number is always even.
\item An even number plus an odd number is never even.
\item An odd number plus an odd number is always even.
\item An even number minus an even number is always even.
\item An even number minus an odd number is never even.
\item An odd number minus an odd number is always even.
\end{enumerate}
<<4>> Give me a fill-in-the-blanks exercise for a student learning German. It should be an exercise on modal verbs.
<<4>> Fill in the correct form of the modal verb in the following sentences.

\begin{enumerate}
\item Wir \_\_\_\_\_ heute in die Stadt. (We must go to the city today.)
\item Du \_\_\_\_\_ das Buch lesen. (You should read this book.)
\item Sie \_\_\_\_\_ in der Nacht auf dem Flughafen ankommen. (They will arrive at the airport at night.)
\item Ich \_\_\_\_\_ in die Schule gehen. (I have to go to school.)
\item Wir \_\_\_\_\_ uns an die Regeln halten. (We have to follow the rules.)
\item Du \_\_\_\_\_ nicht so laut sprechen. (You must not speak so loudly.)
\item Sie \_\_\_\_\_ in der Stadt aufhören. (They have to stop in the city.)
\item Er \_\_\_\_\_ das Haus verlassen. (He has to leave the house.)
\item Sie \_\_\_\_\_ nicht so viele Fragen stellen. (They must not ask so many questions.)
\item Du \_\_\_\_\_ deine Hausaufgaben machen. (You have to do your homework.)
\item Ich \_\_\_\_\_ ins Kino gehen. (I have to go to the movies.)
\item Wir \_\_\_\_\_ ein neues Auto kaufen. (We have to buy a new car.)
\item Sie \_\_\_\_\_ in der Bibliothek lernen. (They have to study in the library.)
\item Du \_\_\_\_\_ deine Eltern anrufen. (You must call your parents.)
\item Er \_\_\_\_\_ seine Prüfung wiederholen. (He has to repeat his exam.)
\end{enumerate}
