<<16>> Give me an algebra exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on evaluating expressions. It should have multiple steps. There should be marks/points assigned to the question. It should be a with Answer.
<<16>> Find the value of each of the following expressions when \( x = 3 \): (2 marks each)

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( 2x + 4 \)
\item \( 5x - 1 \)
\item \( 2x - 5 \)
\item \( 3x + 2 \)
\item \( 7 - 4x \)
\item \( 9 + 6x \)
\item \( 8 + 5x \)
\item \( 2x^2 - 4x + 3 \)
\item \( 3x^2 - 5x - 2 \)
\item \( 4x^2 - 3x + 1 \)
\item \( 2x^2 + 4x - 5 \)
\item \( 5x^2 - 2x - 4 \)
\item \( 6x^2 + 3x - 3 \)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( 2(3) + 4 = 10 \)
\item \( 5(3) - 1 = 14 \)
\item \( 2(3) - 5 = 1 \)
\item \( 3(3) + 2 = 11 \)
\item \( 7 - 4(3) = -5 \)
\item \( 9 + 6(3) = 27 \)
\item \( 8 + 5(3) = 23 \)
\item \( 2(3)^2 - 4(3) + 3 = 2(9) - 12 + 3 = 9 \)
\item \( 3(3)^2 - 5(3) - 2 = 3(9) - 15 - 2 = 14 \)
\item \( 4(3)^2 - 3(3) + 1 = 4(9) - 9 + 1 = 28 \)
\item \( 2(3)^2 + 4(3) - 5 = 2(9) + 12 - 5 = 25 \)
\item \( 5(3)^2 - 2(3) - 4 = 5(9) - 6 - 4 = 37 \)
\item \( 6(3)^2 + 3(3) - 3 = 6(9) + 9 - 3 = 60 \)
\end{enumerate}
