<<80>> Give me a combination of an arithmetic exercise and a word problem for a 2nd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on regrouping. It should have multiple steps.
<<80>> A boy has 4 toy cars. He gets 2 more toy cars. How many toy cars does he have now?

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How many toy cars did the boy have initially?
\item How many toy cars did he get?
\item How many toy cars does he have now?
\end{enumerate}
<<81>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on cost comparison.
<<81>> A book costs \$5. A pen costs \$1. Find the difference in cost between the book and the pen. How much cheaper is the pen than the book? Explain your reasoning. Show your work. Write your answer in the space provided. The difference in cost between the book and the pen is \$ \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ cheaper. The pen is \$ \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ cheaper than the book.
