<<93>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on distance and speed calculation. It should have multiple steps.
<<93>> Tommy drove from his house to a park. The journey took 2 hours and 20 minutes. His average speed for the whole journey was 80 km/h. He drove at an average speed of 120 km/h for \( \frac{3}{5} \) of the journey and at an average speed of 50 km/h for the rest of the journey.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is the total distance of the journey?
\item How long did Tommy drive at an average speed of 120 km/h?
\item How long did Tommy drive at an average speed of 50 km/h?
\end{enumerate}
<<94>> Give me a fill in the blank exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on number statements. It should have multiple steps.
<<94>> Write the missing numbers.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item 1 more than 29 is \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 1 less than 29 is \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 10 more than 29 is \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 10 less than 29 is \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
\end{enumerate}
<<95>> Give me a combination of a creative activity and a drawing exercise for a 1st grade student learning science. It should be an exercise on body parts.
<<95>> Draw a picture of yourself. Label the parts of your body. Draw arrows to show where the parts are located. Use different colours to show different parts of your body. Label them in the correct order. Write the names of the parts on the arrows. Use a ruler to draw straight lines. Show your drawing to the class. Compare it with others. Discuss the similarities and differences. What do you notice about the body parts in your drawings? How do they differ? How are they similar? Share your observations with the class. Write down the names of the body parts you have learned. Use a dictionary or ask a teacher if you need help with spelling. Write the names in alphabetical order. Share your list with the class. Compare your list with others. Discuss the similarities and differences. What do you notice about the lists? How do they differ? How are they similar? Share your observations with the class. Choose one body part and draw a picture of it. Label the drawing with the name of the part. Use a different colour for each letter. Show your drawing to the class. Compare it with others. Discuss the similarities and differences. What do you notice about the drawings? How do they differ? How are they similar? Share your observations with the class. Write a sentence using the name of the body part you chose. Use the sentence in a conversation with a friend or family member. Share the conversation with the class. Discuss how you used the word in context. What did you learn from the activity? Share your thoughts with the class. Write down three things you learned about body parts. Use complete sentences and proper spelling. Share your list with the class. Compare it with others. Discuss the similarities and differences. What do you notice about the lists? How do they differ? How are they similar? Share your observations with the class. Write a short paragraph using three of the body parts you learned. Use complete sentences and proper spelling. Share your paragraph with the cl