\end{itemize}
<<118>> Give me a geometry exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on identifying symmetry. The exercise should contain some kind of a graphic component (illustration, diagram, table, etc).
<<118>> Identify the lines of symmetry in each shape.

[STRDGM] A circle with two lines of symmetry, a triangle with three lines of symmetry, and a square with two lines of symmetry. [STPDGM]
<<119>> Give me an arithmetic exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on equivalent fractions. It should have multiple steps.
<<119>> Find the equivalent fractions for the following:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( \frac{1}{2} \)
\item \( \frac{2}{4} \)
\item \( \frac{3}{6} \)
\end{enumerate}
<<120>> Give me a question exercise for a 6th grade student learning science. It should have a subsection for materials. It should be an exercise on mass and weight. It should be a with Answer.
<<120>> What is the difference between mass and weight?

\subsection*{Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item A scale
\item Various objects
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{itemize}
\item Mass is a measure of the amount of matter in an object, while weight is a measure of the force of gravity acting on that object.
\end{itemize}
