<<152>> Give me an arithmetic exercise for a 5th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on volume calculation. It should be a with Answer.
<<152>> Find the volume of the following liquids in millilitres:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item 0.25 L
\item 0.5 L
\item 0.75 L
\item 1 L
\item 1.25 L
\item 1.5 L
\item 1.75 L
\item 2 L
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item 250 mL
\item 500 mL
\item 750 mL
\item 1000 mL
\item 1250 mL
\item 1500 mL
\item 1750 mL
\item 2000 mL
\end{enumerate}
