<<243>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on time calculations. It should have multiple steps.
<<243>> The train from City A to City B took 6 hours and 30 minutes. The train from City B to City C took 3 hours and 15 minutes. The train from City C to City D took 5 hours and 20 minutes. The train from City D to City E took 2 hours and 40 minutes.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is the total time taken for the journey from City A to City B?
\item What is the total time taken for the journey from City B to City C?
\item What is the total time taken for the journey from City C to City D?
\item What is the total time taken for the journey from City D to City E?
\item What is the total time taken for the entire journey from City A to City E?
\end{enumerate}
