<<275>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should have a subsection for answers. It should be an exercise on percentages.
<<275>> A factory produced 1000 boxes of soap. 120 boxes of soap were sold. What percentage of the boxes of soap were not sold?

\subsection*{Answers}
The percentage of boxes not sold is 88\%. This is calculated by subtracting the percentage of boxes sold (12\%) from 100\%. The percentage of boxes sold is found by dividing the number of boxes sold (120) by the total number of boxes (1000) and then multiplying by 100. This gives 12\%. Subtracting this from 100\% gives 88\%.
