<<484>> Give me a combination of a short answer exercise and a group activity for a 5th grade student learning geography.
<<484>> Work with a friend to prepare a class display of pictures and information about a large river. Write a sentence or two to explain what each picture shows. Choose a river from a country other than your own. Use reference books or the Internet to help you. You could choose the River Nile, the River Amazon, the River Mekong or the River Yangtze. If you can, include pictures of the river in different seasons and in different parts of its course. Choose some pictures of the river's floodplains, deltas, lakes and waterfalls. Find out about the river's source, its length, its uses, and the problems it causes. Include some pictures of the people who live and work along the river. Find out what goods are transported along the river and what the river is used for. Add some pictures of the river's wildlife. If you have the opportunity, try to visit the river and take some pictures yourself. Then you can add these to your display. When you have finished your display, tell the class what you have found out. Use your pictures to help you. Try to answer the following questions:  
\begin{enumerate}
\item Where does the river rise?  
\item Where does the river flow into the sea?  
\item What are the river's main tributaries?  
\item How do people use the river?  
\item What are the river's main problems?  
\item What wildlife lives in the river and along its banks?  
\item What goods are transported along the river?  
\end{enumerate}
