<<499>> In the Stone Age, people made tools from:  
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item wood and bone  
\item wood and stone  
\item bone and stone  
\end{enumerate}   The correct answer is: \begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]  
\item wood and bone  
\end{enumerate}   The Stone Age is divided into three periods:  
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Bronze, Iron and Roman  
\item Old, Middle and New  
\item Stone, Bronze and Iron  
\end{enumerate}   The correct answer is: \begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]  
\item Old, Middle and New  
\end{enumerate}   The Old Stone Age is also known as:  
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item the Palaeolithic Age  
\item the Mesolithic Age  
\item the Neolithic Age  
\end{enumerate}   The correct answer is: \begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]  
\item the Palaeolithic Age  
