<<502>> Give me a combination of a creative exercise and a writing exercise for a 2nd grade student learning English.
<<502>> Draw and write about the following:
\begin{enumerate}
\item your favourite animal
\item your best friend
\item a place you would like to visit
\item something you would like to be when you grow up
\end{enumerate}
<<503>> Give me a combination of a drawing exercise and a writing exercise for a 5th grade student learning geography.
<<503>> \begin{enumerate}
\item Choose a busy street in your area. Write a list of all the shops, services and other buildings in that street.  
\item Draw a sketch plan of the street.  
\item Write a sentence or two to explain why you think the street is so busy.  
\end{enumerate}  .
<<504>> Give me a combination of a fill in the blank exercise and a counting exercise for a 2nd grade student learning mathematics.
<<504>> Complete the number sentences. Write the missing number word.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item 3 more than 25 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 2 less than 31 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 1 more than 34 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 4 less than 29 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\end{enumerate}
<<505>> Give me a vocabulary exercise for a 6th grade student learning English.
<<505>> \begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Write a word that is similar to each of these words. The words are similar in meaning to the words in the list, but are more formal.
    \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
    \item walk \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item run \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item jump \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item swim \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item shout \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item smile \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item cry \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item talk \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item laugh \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item wave \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \end{enumerate}

\item Use two of the words from the list in sentences of your own.
    \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
    \item \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \item \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
    \end{enumerate}
\end{enumerate}
