<<507>> Give me a punctuation exercise for a 1st grade student learning English.
<<507>> Add the missing speech marks to the following sentences.
\begin{enumerate}
\item I am a rabbit, said the rabbit.
\item I am a cat, said the cat.
\item I am a dog, said the dog.
\item I am a hen, said the hen.
\item I am a duck, said the duck.
\end{enumerate}
<<508>> Give me a combination of an estimating exercise and a temporal exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics.
<<508>> Estimate the time it takes to complete each of the following activities:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Eating a meal: \_\_\_ minutes
\item Doing homework: \_\_\_ minutes
\item Walking to school: \_\_\_ minutes
\item Reading a book: \_\_\_ minutes
\item Sleeping: \_\_\_ hours
\end{enumerate}
