<<524>> Give me a short answer exercise for a 3rd grade student learning geography.
<<524>> Write a list of the things you would like to do in the countryside. Then write a list of the things you would not like to do in the countryside. Think about the people who live and work in the countryside. How would your ideas affect them? Would your ideas help the countryside to be a nice place to live and work? Would they help to protect the countryside for the future? Try to think of ways in which you could enjoy the countryside without spoiling it. Write down your ideas. Try to think of ways in which you could enjoy the countryside without spoiling it. Write down your ideas. Share your ideas with a friend or family member. Do they have any ideas that you could add to your list? Now share your ideas with the class and make a class display of your ideas. Use your ideas to write a letter or make a poster telling people how to enjoy the countryside without spoiling it. Share your work with the class. Choose one of the ideas and make a model of it. For example, you could make a model of a bird hide or a footpath. Share your model with the class. Now use reference books or the Internet to find out about the countryside in other countries. How is it different from the countryside in your country? How is it similar? Share your ideas with the class. Write a list of the things you would like to do in the countryside. Then write a list of the things you would not like to do in the countryside. Think about the people who live and work in the countryside. How would your ideas affect them? Would your ideas help the countryside to be a nice place to live and work? Would they help to protect the countryside for the future? Try to think of ways in which you could enjoy the countryside without spoiling it. Write down your ideas. Try to think of ways in which you could enjoy the countryside without spoiling it. Write down your ideas. Share your ideas with a friend or family member. Do they have any ideas that you could add to your list? Now share your ideas with the class 