<<541>> Give me a combination of a research exercise and an activity for a 2nd grade student learning geography.
<<541>> Look at some old photographs or postcards of your local area. Write down all the changes you can see. Have any of the buildings disappeared? Are there new buildings? Has the land use changed? Are there more cars and lorries? Are there more people? Are the clothes and hairstyles different? What other changes can you see? Write a paragraph describing what life was like in the past in your area. Try to imagine what it would have been like to live in your area at that time. Think about what the air would have been like, what the traffic would have been like, and how noisy it would have been. Think about what people would have been doing in the photographs. What jobs would they have had? What would they have been doing in their free time? What games would they have played? What music would they have listened to? How would they have travelled? How would they have communicated? Write a paragraph describing what life was like in the past in your area. Try to imagine what it would have been like to live in your area at that time. Think about what the air would have been like, what the traffic would have been like, and how noisy it would have been. Think about what people would have been doing in the photographs. What jobs would they have had? What would they have been doing in their free time? What games would they have played? What music would they have listened to? How would they have travelled? How would they have communicated? Write a paragraph describing what life was like in the past in your area. Try to imagine what it would have been like to live in your area at that time. Think about what the air would have been like, what the traffic would have been like, and how noisy it would have been. Think about what people would have been doing in the photographs. What jobs would they have had? What would they have been doing in their free time? What games would they have played? What music would they have listened to? How would they have travelled? How would they hav