<<555>> Give me a measurement exercise for a 2nd grade student learning mathematics.
<<555>> Use a pencil or a book as 1 unit to measure the following objects:
\begin{itemize}
\item A pencil case
\item A book
\item A pencil
\end{itemize} 
Write the length of each object in the table below.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
\textbf{Object} & \textbf{Length} \\
\hline
Pencil case &  \\
\hline
Book &  \\
\hline
Pencil &  \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
