<<574>> Give me a combination of a writing exercise and a sentence formation exercise for a student learning Dutch. It should have a subsection for answers. It should be an exercise involving an example. It should be an exercise on giving negative answers.
<<574>> Give a negative answer to the following questions, using the words provided in brackets.\\
For example: Wil je met me mee? (naar de bioscoop)\\
Nee, ik ga niet naar de bioscoop.

\begin{enumerate}
\item Wil je met me mee? (naar de bioscoop)
\item Wil je met me mee? (naar de stad)
\item Wil je met me mee? (naar de kroeg)
\item Wil je met me mee? (naar het feest)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Nee, ik ga niet naar de bioscoop.
\item Nee, ik ga niet naar de stad.
\item Nee, ik ga niet naar de kroeg.
\item Nee, ik ga niet naar het feest.
\end{enumerate}
<<575>> Give me a combination of a question exercise and a partner discussion for a 6th grade student learning science. It should be an exercise on mass and weight. The exercise should contain some kind of a graphic component (illustration, diagram, table, etc).
<<575>> \begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Look at the scales and balances shown. Discuss with your group how you think they work.
\item Can you remember how to measure mass? What are the units of mass?
\item Look at the scales and balances shown. Can you see how they are used to measure mass?
\item Discuss with your group how to find the weight of an object. What are the units of weight?
\item Look at the scales and balances shown. Can you see how they are used to measure weight?
\end{enumerate}

[STRDGM] The image shows various scales and balances, including a spring scale, a digital scale, and an old-fashioned balance scale. Each scale is designed to measure mass or weight in different units. [STPDGM]
