\end{enumerate}
<<592>> Give me a grammar exercise for a student learning Spanish. It should be an exercise on completing sentences. It should be a with Answer.
<<592>> Complete the following sentences with the correct form of the verb in brackets.  
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Yo (tomar) \_\_\_\_\_ un café todos los días. (I have a coffee every day.)
    \item Él (comer) \_\_\_\_\_ muy bien. (He eats very well.)
    \item Ella (trabajar) \_\_\_\_\_ en una empresa. (She works in a company.)
    \item Ellos (vivir) \_\_\_\_\_ en Madrid. (They live in Madrid.)
    \item Yo (salir) \_\_\_\_\_ a las 7. (I leave at 7.)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item tomo
\item come
\item trabaja
\item viven
\item salgo
\end{enumerate}
