<<604>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on cost calculation. It should be a with Answer.
<<604>> The cost of a watch is \$60. If a 10\% discount is given, what is the selling price of the watch?

\subsection*{Answers}
The selling price of the watch is \$54.00. This is calculated by subtracting 10\% of the original price from the original price: \( 60 - (0.10 \times 60) = 60 - 6 = 54 \). Alternatively, you can find 90\% of the original price: \( 0.90 \times 60 = 54 \). Both methods yield the same result.
