<<628>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on percentage calculation. It should be a with Answer.
<<628>> There were 40,000 people at a concert. 16,000 of them were men. What percentage of the people at the concert were women?

\subsection*{Answers}
The percentage of women at the concert is 60\%. This is calculated by subtracting the percentage of men from 100\%, since 16,000 out of 40,000 are men, which is 40\%. So, 100\% - 40\% = 60\%. This means that 60\% of the people at the concert were women.
<<629>> Give me an arithmetic exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving division. It should be a with Answer.
<<629>> Divide 360 by 6.

\subsection*{Answers}
The answer is 60. The remainder is 0. The quotient is 60. The divisor is 6. The dividend is 360. The quotient times the divisor is 60 times 6, which equals 360. The dividend is equal to the quotient times the divisor. The remainder is 0, indicating that there is no remainder. Therefore, the division of 360 by 6 results in 60 with no remainder.
