<<666>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should have multiple steps.
<<666>> A fruit seller packed 450 apples into bags of 6 each. He packed 8 bags.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How many apples did he pack in total?
\item How many apples were left over?
\end{enumerate}
<<667>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should have multiple steps.
<<667>> Lily had 3000 stamps. She gave 600 stamps to her brother and 1200 stamps to her sister. How many stamps did she have left?

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How many stamps did Lily give away in total?
\item How many stamps did Lily have left after giving away the stamps?
\end{enumerate}
<<668>> Give me a combination of an arithmetic exercise, a word problem, and a fill in the blank exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should have multiple steps.
<<668>> Write the missing numbers:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item 1 km = \_\_\_\_\_ m
\item 1 m = \_\_\_\_\_ cm
\item 1 cm = \_\_\_\_\_ mm
\end{enumerate}
<<669>> Give me a combination of a fill in the blank exercise and an arithmetic exercise for a 1st grade student learning mathematics. It should have multiple steps.
