<<677>> Give me a combination of a counting exercise and a matching exercise for a 1st grade student learning mathematics. The exercise should contain some kind of a graphic component (illustration, diagram, table, etc). It should have multiple steps.
<<677>> Count the number of each type of fruit. Write the total number of fruits. Draw a circle around the greatest number. Draw a circle around the smallest number.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How many apples are there?
\item How many bananas are there?
\item How many oranges are there?
\item How many grapes are there?
\item What is the total number of fruits?
\item Which type of fruit has the greatest number?
\item Which type of fruit has the smallest number?
\end{enumerate}

[STRDGM] A grid showing 5 apples, 3 bananas, 4 oranges, and 2 grapes. [STPDGM]
