<<695>> Give me a combination of a discussion exercise and a group activity for a 3rd grade student learning computer science.
<<695>> Talk to a friend about your computer use at home. Discuss the following topics: 
\begin{itemize}
\item how often you use a computer at home
\item the types of activities you do on the computer
\item how you use computers for learning
\end{itemize} 
Describe your experience of using computers in your daily life. Think about the ways you use technology, such as playing games, using the internet, and creating documents. Share your thoughts with your friend. Then, talk about how you can use computers for learning. Discuss ways you can use computers to help you with your school work. Think about the tools and resources you can use, such as word processors, spreadsheets, and educational software. Share your ideas with your friend. Finally, discuss ways you can use computers for learning outside of school. Think about how you can use computers to learn new skills, explore different subjects, and access educational resources. Share your ideas with your friend. Now, think about how you can use computers to learn more about a subject you are interested in. Choose a topic that you enjoy, such as science, history, or art. Think about the ways you can use computers to learn more about this subject, such as watching videos, reading articles, and playing educational games. Share your ideas with your friend. Finally, discuss ways you can use computers to learn a new skill. Think about the tools and resources you can use, such as online tutorials, educational software, and apps. Share your ideas with your friend. Describe your experience of using computers in your daily life. Think about the ways you use technology, such as playing games, using the internet, and creating documents. Share your thoughts with your friend. Then, talk about how you can use computers for learning. Discuss ways you can use computers to help you with your school work. Think about the tools and resources you can use, such as word processors, spreadsheets, and educational software. Share your ideas with your friend. Finally, discuss ways you can use computers for learning outside of school. Think about how you can use computers to learn new skills, explore different subjects, and access educational resources. Share your ideas with your friend. Now, thin