ilar interests in animals? Think about how you can use computers to learn about plants. What are some ways you can use computers to learn about different plant species and their habitats? How can you use computers to find and view information about plants? What are some ways you can use computers to create presentations and reports about plant topics? How can you use computers to connect with others who share similar interests in plants? Think about how you can use computers to learn about food production. What are some ways you can use computers to learn about farming and agriculture? How can you use computers to find and view information about food production? What are some ways you can use computers to create presentations and reports about food production topics? How can you use computers to connect with others who share similar interests in food production? Think about how you can use computers to learn about the economy. What are some ways you can use computers to learn about different economic systems and concepts? How can you use computers to find and view economic information and resources? What are some ways you can use computers to create presentations and reports about economic topics? How can you use computers to connect with others who share similar interests in economics? Think about how you can use computers to learn about government. What are some ways you can use computers to learn about different types of government and political systems? How can you use computers to find and view information about government? What are some ways you can use computers to create presentations and reports about government topics? How can you use computers to connect with others who share similar interests in government? Think about how you can use computers to learn about the media. What are some ways you can use computers to learn about different types of media and their roles in society? How can you use computers to find and view information about the media? What a