<<705>> Fill in the blanks for the following equations:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( 8 + 4 = \_\_\_ \)
\item \( 6 + 7 = \_\_\_ \)
\end{enumerate}
<<706>> Give me a combination of a fill in the blank exercise and an arithmetic exercise for a 1st grade student learning mathematics.
<<706>> Fill in the missing numbers:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\Roman*.]
\item 4 less than 24 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 10 less than 24 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 4 more than 24 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item 10 more than 24 is \_\_\_\_\_\_.
\end{enumerate}
