\end{enumerate}
<<709>> Give me a combination of a research exercise and a short answer exercise for a 3rd grade student learning geography.
<<709>> \begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Choose a place in a hot desert that you have never visited. Find out as much as you can about it from reference books or the Internet. Write a list of the things you discover.
\item Which of the following things could you do to help people living in that place?
\begin{itemize}
\item Send food and clothes to people who have lost their homes.
\item Help to build new homes for people.
\item Tell people about the problems caused by sand dunes.
\item Send money to help people.
\end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}
<<710>> Give me a combination of a research exercise, a short answer exercise, and an activity for a 5th grade student learning computer science.
<<710>> \begin{enumerate}
\item Find a news article or a website that talks about the impact of human activity on the environment. 
\item Write down what the article says. 
\item Choose one way in which humans harm the environment and describe it in detail. 
\end{enumerate}
<<711>> Give me a combination of a short answer exercise, a writing exercise, and an activity for a 5th grade student learning geography.
<<711>> Imagine that you are a member of a local authority that is considering whether to allow a new airport to be built. Write a report to the authority with your recommendations. Think about the following points:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Will the airport create many jobs for local people?
\item Will the airport increase noise pollution and traffic problems?
\item Will the airport bring more tourists and businesses to the area?
\end{enumerate} Write your report using the headings below.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Introduction
\item Advantages of the airport
\item Disadvantages of the airport
\item Conclusion
\end{enumerate}
