<<724>> Give me a combination of a research exercise, a mapping exercise, and an activity for a 5th grade student learning geography. It should have a subsection for materials.
<<724>> \begin{enumerate}
\item Choose a city or large town to study.
\item Collect a large-scale map of your chosen place.
\item Find out as much as you can about the place.
\item Mark the main features, such as the city or town centre, railway stations, parks and green spaces, river or sea coast, roads and motorways, and the airport, on your map.
\item Choose one area on your map that is near the city or town centre. Find out what the land is used for there. Is it housing, factories, offices, shops or something else?
\item Draw a sketch map of the area.
\item Find out what the land was used for in the past.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Large-scale map of a city or large town
\end{itemize}
