<<753>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on speed calculation. It should have multiple steps.
<<753>> The average speed of a car for the whole journey was 75 km/h. The average speed of the car from Town A to Town B was 80 km/h. The average speed of the car from Town B to Town C was 65 km/h. If the distance from Town A to Town B was 240 km, what was the distance from Town B to Town C?

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is the total distance traveled from Town A to Town C?
\item What is the distance from Town B to Town C?
\end{enumerate}
