\item If \( r = 4 \), find the number of people sitting.
\item If \( r = 8 \), find the number of people sitting.
\end{enumerate}
<<756>> Give me a word scramble exercise for a student learning Dutch. It should have a subsection for answers, and hints.
<<756>> All the letters of these words are jumbled up. Rearrange the letters so that they make meaningful words.
\begin{enumerate}
\item nloee
\item jee
\item nve
\item oot
\item nve
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Hints}
\begin{enumerate}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{o}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{all}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{z}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{sea}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{v}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{in}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{t}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{to}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{v}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{in}
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item alle
\item zee
\item in
\item tot
\item in
\end{enumerate}
<<757>> Give me a combination of a discussion exercise and a question exercise for a 3rd grade student learning science. It should be an exercise on materials. The exercise should contain some kind of a graphic component (illustration, diagram, table, etc).
<<757>> \begin{itemize}
\item Discuss with your group the different materials that can be used to make a bag. Write down the materials that you think are best.
\item Why are some materials better than others for making bags?
\item Why are some materials not suitable for making bags?
\item Can you think of any materials that would be very good for making bags but have not been used yet?
\item Which material do you think is the best for making a bag?
\item Try to give reasons for your choice.
\item Share your ideas with the class.
\end{itemize}

[STRDGM] The image shows various types of bags made from different materials, including a leather handbag, a cloth tote bag, a paper bag, and a plastic bag. Each bag is labeled with its material type. [STPDGM]
<<758>> Give me a grammar exercise for a student learning French. It should be an exercise on conjugation. It should be a with Answer.
<<758>> Mettre au futur simple les verbes entre parenthèses.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Il (répondre)          à toutes vos questions.
    \item Ils (acheter)          un nouvel ordinateur.
    \item Je (préférer)          un café noir.
    \item Il (faire)          un voyage en Russie.
    \item Nous (compléter)          tous les exercices.
    \item Il (finir)          son livre.
    \item Nous (aller)          au Japon.
    \item Il (devenir)          le nouveau président.
    \item Elle (recevoir)          un prix littéraire.
    \item Il (se marier)          avec sa fiancée.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item répondra
\item achèteront
\item préférerai
\item fera
\item compléterons
\item finira
\item irons
\item deviendra
\item recevra
\item se mariera
\end{enumerate}
