<<759>> Give two positive and two negative adjectives for the following nouns.\\
For example:\\
het huis (the house)\\
positieve bijvoeglijke naamwoorden: mooi, comfortabel\\
negatieve bijvoeglijke naamwoorden: saai, klein\\

\begin{enumerate}
\item het land
\item het water
\item de stad
\item het weer
\end{enumerate}
<<760>> Give me a word completion exercise for a student learning Dutch. It should have a subsection for answers, and hints. It should be an exercise on guessing words.
<<760>> Guess the word in each case; some of the letters have been hidden by the underscore ( \_ ) sign.
\begin{enumerate}
\item a\_r\_r\_n
\item p\_r\_e\_
\item z\_e\_m\_n
\item a\_n\_v\_n
\item v\_r\_s\_h\_l
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Hints}

\begin{enumerate}
\item The second letter of the answer is \emph{r}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{arrange}
\item The second letter of the answer is \emph{r}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{prepare}
\item The second letter of the answer is \emph{o}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{swim}
\item The second letter of the answer is \emph{a}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{use}
\item The second letter of the answer is \emph{o}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{prevent}
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item arranger
\item prepare
\item zwemmen
\item gebruiken
\item voorkomen
\end{enumerate}
