<<774>> Give me an arithmetic exercise for a 4th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving multiplication. It should be an exercise involving division.
<<774>> Write two multiplication sentences and two division sentences for each number. Use 2, 5, and 10 as your divisors.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item For 20: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 4 \times 5 = 20 \)
   \item Division: \( 40 \div 2 = 20 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 10 \times 2 = 20 \)
   \item Division: \( 100 \div 5 = 20 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 30: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 6 \times 5 = 30 \)
   \item Division: \( 60 \div 2 = 30 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 15 \times 2 = 30 \)
   \item Division: \( 150 \div 5 = 30 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 40: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 8 \times 5 = 40 \)
   \item Division: \( 80 \div 2 = 40 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 20 \times 2 = 40 \)
   \item Division: \( 200 \div 5 = 40 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 50: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 10 \times 5 = 50 \)
   \item Division: \( 100 \div 2 = 50 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 25 \times 2 = 50 \)
   \item Division: \( 250 \div 5 = 50 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 60: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 12 \times 5 = 60 \)
   \item Division: \( 120 \div 2 = 60 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 30 \times 2 = 60 \)
   \item Division: \( 300 \div 5 = 60 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 70: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 14 \times 5 = 70 \)
   \item Division: \( 140 \div 2 = 70 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 35 \times 2 = 70 \)
   \item Division: \( 350 \div 5 = 70 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 80: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 16 \times 5 = 80 \)
   \item Division: \( 160 \div 2 = 80 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 40 \times 2 = 80 \)
   \item Division: \( 400 \div 5 = 80 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 90: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 18 \times 5 = 90 \)
   \item Division: \( 180 \div 2 = 90 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 45 \times 2 = 90 \)
   \item Division: \( 450 \div 5 = 90 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\item For 100: 
   \begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
   \item Multiplication: \( 20 \times 5 = 100 \)
   \item Division: \( 200 \div 2 = 100 \)
   \item Multiplication: \( 50 \times 2 = 100 \)
   \item Division: \( 500 \div 5 = 100 \)
   \end{enumerate}
\end{enumerate}
<<775>> Give me an arithmetic exercise for a 5th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving division. It should have multiple steps. It should be a with Answer.
